# base_unittests tests that fail on a FAT /data and pass on an ext one (tools/cr-test.sh base,
# tools/cr/base-run.py adds this list to base_unittests.skip when the stick's /data is FAT;
# same format). Made 2026-10-16 (CB2b, docs/CR-PLAN.md "CB2b on ext") from the 54 tests
# CB2's file-system group listed: these 44 pass on ext (extfs keeps symlinks, modes, owners and
# times, finds a file unlinked while open by its name no longer, and enforces the open
# mode); the 10 that still fail on ext are in base_unittests.skip with the layer that owns them.

[fs] /data is FAT: symlink(), mkfifo(), chmod bits and utimensat are not kept; a file unlinked while open is still found; read-only/write-only flags are not enforced (the ENOSYS log's ioctl 0x80086601 is FS_IOC_GETFLAGS)
